PROJECT TITLE
Deploying a Scalable Static Website with a CDN

DESCRIPTION
This project demonstrates the deployment of a static website using Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront (CDN). The website is hosted on Amazon S3, while CloudFront provides faster content delivery, improved performance, and high availability.

OBJECTIVES
• Host a static website on Amazon S3.
• Configure bucket permissions for public access.
• Enable Static Website Hosting.
• Integrate Amazon CloudFront as a Content Delivery Network.
• Verify successful deployment.

TECHNOLOGIES USED
• Amazon S3
• Amazon CloudFront
• HTML

IMPLEMENTATION STEPS
1. Created an Amazon S3 bucket.
2. Uploaded the website files.
3. Enabled Static Website Hosting.
4. Configured the bucket policy.
5. Created an Amazon CloudFront distribution.
6. Configured the Default Root Object as index.html.
7. Successfully deployed and tested the website.

FEATURES
• Static website hosting
• Fast content delivery using CDN
• Public accessibility
• Improved website performance

